; ============================================================================
; LAD GEM per-APV-card gain-match constants (both modules, all U and V cards)
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Source : APV gain calibration with LAD proton hits (C3 target, SHMS 13.5 deg),
;          U/V charge asymmetry method as in SBS-replay GEM_GainMatch.C, robust per-hit fit.
;          Report: apv_calibration_report.pdf (lad_replay_apvs_calibration)
; Model  : ADC_measured = C * ADC_true for every strip read by the card.
;          C is relative to U card pos 4 of the same module (C = 1).
; Stored : lgem_mN_ugain / lgem_mN_vgain = 1/C  (THcLADGEMModule MULTIPLIES the strip ADC by
;          fUgain / fVgain[strip/128], so 1/C brings every card to the scale of U pos 4).
; Index  : card position 'pos' of MAPS/LAD/DETEC/GEM/lgem_chan.map: 12 U cards (0-11),
;          24 V cards (0-23) per module.
; Origin of each value (column 'src' in the tables below):
;   S3  = main fit on the clean sample (>= 30 hits)                       51 of 72 cards
;   S2  = same fit on the larger sample S2 (>= 100 hits, error <= 10 %),
;         rescaled to the S3 scale (x1.011 GEM0, x0.990 GEM1)              5 of 72 cards
;   avg = no protons reach the card: average C of the calibrated cards of
;         the same axis and module (not a measurement)                    16 of 72 cards
;         (GEM1 V pos 17 is a dead card)
;
; !!! STATUS: THcLADGEMModule (LADlib, checked 2026-11-17) does NOT yet read lgem_mN_ugain /
; lgem_mN_vgain: fUgain / fVgain are set to 1 (times lgem_modulegain) for every card. These
; keys only take effect after LADlib loads them (DBRequest {"_ugain", ...}, {"_vgain", ...}
; with prefix "lgem_mN" in THcLADGEMModule::ReadDatabase).
; Note: zero suppression is applied before the gain, but lgem_threshold_sample / _stripsum /
; _clustersum are applied after it, so the overall normalisation (U pos 4 = 1, V cards scaled
; by ~0.5) changes which V strips/clusters pass those thresholds. Re-check them when enabling.
; ============================================================================

